            {
              "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
              "Text": "**Supplement store**\r\n\r\nThe script GrazeForageCrop allows for optional supplementary feeding. In order to support that feeding it is necessary to include the Supplement model in the simulation. All the buying and feeding out is handled in GrazeForageCrop but here we name the supplement (“silage”) and give it some properties including the quality parameters of the supplement. \r\n\r\nIn the quality parameters, note that we set the dry matter percentage to 100. This is does not affect the feeding quality of the supplement but means that all buy, sell, feed, etc. commands are given on a dry matter rather than wet matter basis. Once these quality parameters are set against a named supplement they are retained and all that is needed is to buy, sell or feed the named supplement. \r\n\r\n",
              "Name": "SupplementMemo",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
            },
            {
              "$type": "Models.GrazPlan.Stock, Models",
              "randFactory": {
                "$type": "StdUnits.MyRandom, Models"
              },
              "RandSeed": 9999,
              "Name": "Stock",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
            },
            {
