              ],
              "Name": "Supplement operations",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "The Supplement operation file is based on pasture/supplement data from the LUDF dataset (see the Validation memo for details).  For the Supplement operations, there are six types of supplements labelled \"silage_11me\", \"pasture_11.5me\", \"pasture_12me\", \"pasture_12.5me\", \"pasture_13me\", and \"pasture_13.5me\" that are bought at the start of the simulation. An excess amount, expressed in kilograms, of each supplement is bought - enough to last longer than the simulation (2E+18 kg in the LUDF validation) and their characteristics must be specified in the Supplement node. The LUDF dataset is based on weekly reports - the daily pasture and supplements supplied (and their characteristics such as ME content) listed in the Supplement operations was extrapolated from the weekly data to the intervening days.\r\n\r\nTo specify the buy and feeding out in the Supplement operation file the following can be used:\r\n\r\n* to buy: \"2004-09-04 [Supplement].Buy(2E+18,\"pasture_13.5me\")\" (without enclosing quotation marks) where \"2004-09-04\" is the date of the operation, and \"[Supplement].Buy(2E+18,\"pasture_13.5me\")\" is to buy 2E+18 kg of supplement type \"pasture_13.5me\". Remember that type of supplement must be specified in the Supplement node.\r\n\r\n* to feed out: \"2004-09-04 [Supplement].Feed(\"pasture_13me\",3861,\"Feedlot\")\" (without enclosing quotation marks) where \"2004-09-04\" is the date of the operation and \"[Supplement].Feed(\"pasture_13me\",3861,\"Feedlot\")\" means to feed out 3861 kg of supplement \"pasture_13me\". Again, the fed out supplement must be specified in the Supplement node.\r\n",
                  "Name": "Supplement operations memo",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                }
              ],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
            },
